# An allow-list, because the build context is everything the Dockerfile CAN
# copy: the whole working tree, ignored and untracked files included. The .git
# directory alone is 16 MB in this checkout — history the image has no use for —
# and a working tree also carries whatever local directories its owner keeps in
# it, none of which the build has any business reading. The image needs two
# files. Anything added to the repository later is excluded until somebody says
# otherwise here, which is the direction that fails safe.
*
!ccdad
!ccdad-entrypoint
